### Guide §5.10 Kafka. VS Code REST Client syntax: click "Send Request" above each request.
### Start the app with the dev profile: it switches Kafka on (library.kafka.enabled), and compose.yaml
### starts the broker next to PostgreSQL:
###   ./mvnw -pl spring-app spring-boot:run -Dspring-boot.run.profiles=dev
### Ids and statuses assume the demo data on an empty database, and a first run of this file: reset
### with docker compose -f spring-app/compose.yaml down -v
### The demo loans are inserted by SQL, not borrowed, so they never went through Kafka: the stats
### start empty. They also start empty after every restart (the consumer counts in memory).

@host = http://localhost:8080

# @name login
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "librarian@library.test", "password": "demo-password"}

### The stats before any borrow (200, [])
GET {{host}}/api/stats/loans
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Alan borrows Pride and Prejudice (201). After the commit, LoanEventPublisher sends it to the
### library.loans topic with key "5" (the book id)
POST {{host}}/api/loans
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"bookId": 5, "memberId": 2}

### Grace borrows it too (201): same key, same partition, so the two stay in order
POST {{host}}/api/loans
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"bookId": 5, "memberId": 3}

### Grace borrows Cosmos (201): another key, maybe another partition
POST {{host}}/api/loans
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"bookId": 8, "memberId": 3}

### Ada asks for The Dispossessed, whose only copy Alan has (409). The borrow is refused before any
### event is raised, so nothing is published. (A loan whose transaction rolls back after the event is
### never published either: LoanKafkaIT.aRolledBackLoanIsNeverPublished)
POST {{host}}/api/loans
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"bookId": 4, "memberId": 1}

### What the consumer has counted (200): [{"bookId":5,"loans":2},{"bookId":8,"loans":1}]. The
### consumer runs on its own thread: a request sent right after a borrow may come a moment too soon
GET {{host}}/api/stats/loans
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Log in as Ada, a member (200)
# @name ada
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "ada@library.test", "password": "demo-password"}

### The stats are for librarians (403)
GET {{host}}/api/stats/loans
Authorization: Bearer {{ada.response.body.accessToken}}

### To look inside the broker, print the topic's messages (key, then JSON value) with the Kafka tools in
### the container. A shell command, not an HTTP request; it stops after 10 s without a new message:
###   docker compose -f spring-app/compose.yaml exec kafka /opt/kafka/bin/kafka-console-consumer.sh --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 --topic library.loans --from-beginning --formatter-property print.key=true --timeout-ms 10000
